**Read:** [Organic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../sources/Organic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_1ERYESBGNKCKMDY0NPHJKCVJG0), the complete synthesis-gas/methanol process teaching; [Chemical Technology: From Principles to Products — Jess and Wasserscheid](../sources/Chemical-Technology-Jess-Wasserscheid.lingua#r_38DBBMW0BMR89K3R95V073YA41), the entire syngas-to-methanol industrial example if using the commercial text; [Industrial Chemical Technology II — Nduka, NOUN](../sources/Industrial-Chemical-Technology-II-NOUN.lingua#r_7RXE2GF1DW7QH9GHTCGT0P09SR), the whole synthesis-feed and process-route context; [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the complete relevant equilibrium, rates and reactor-energy treatments.

Methanol synthesis can involve CO+2H₂⇌CH₃OH and CO₂+3H₂⇌CH₃OH+H₂O together with other reactions such as shift. Feed composition, activities, catalyst state, temperature and finite rates affect the outcome. A nominal hydrogen-to-carbon ratio alone cannot establish the actual reacting state.

For a simplified combined carbon-oxide feed balance, the commonly useful ratio (H₂−CO₂)/(CO+CO₂) equals two at stoichiometric supply under the stated methanol-forming relations. This algebraic index is not a complete equilibrium, kinetic or circulation model; actual contaminants, purge and product removal need separate accounts.

Reaction heat, compression, condensation, distillation, water and impurity pathways shape useful methanol output. A changed carbon source can alter upstream energy/purification and downstream water duties even when the final molecule is the same. Preserve observed and projected performance separately.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public methanol route with actual feed and product evidence. Independently close carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, water, heat and recycle/purge, then compare a justified alternative feed or operating arrangement on the same accepted product. Explain which model/data uncertainty most affects the result and what evidence would discriminate competing claims.

